EP  - 34
DO  - 10.1093/aesa/70.1.31
AB  - Populations of Carabidae were studied in 3 different woodland communities (5 study habitats) in Arkansas. Lists of the species collected in each habitat are given. Five species were collected in numbers large enough to warrant forming conslusions about their seasonal activity. These were Evarthrus convivus LeConte, E. parasodalis Freitag, E. seximpressus LeConte, Pterostichus permundus (Say) (Carabidae: Carabinae: Pterostichini), and Pasimachus elongatus LeConte (Carabidae: Carabinae: Scaritini). These 5 species are referred to as “dominants” in the habitats in which they occur in large numbers. It is postulated that these species utilize most of the resources available to the ground beetle element of the community and thereby exclude large numbers of other ground beetle species.
